Can we do better than 1-shot?
 0-shot learning : trains the model based on class attributes instead of data examples
 Ex.: match tree images with the properties of different trees species  LO-shot (less-than-one-shot!) learning : trains the model with distilled soft-labeled data
 Initially, the probabilities of belonging to the available classes are used to partition the solution space. Then, new partitions are created for unseen before data  Ex.: a k-NN classifier with N initial classes will have its space partitioned into M > N regions
